WEBVTT

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.730
Look at his eyes.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.490
He has the eyes of a fox.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.950
Look at your eyes.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.660
You have the mouth of a crocodile.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.660
Grandfather!

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:46.830
Come now.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.000
The sun is setting.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.420
Let's go home.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.920
Grandfather, why do the people
in the village bow to us?

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.180
That's because we are the guardian
gods of the village.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.470
Why can't we talk with them?

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:08.690
That's because gods must not speak with people casually.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:12.770
What about to thank them
for giving us food every day?

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.900
I'll tell them that.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.370
I don't like being lonely.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.660
It's all right, Kuchiha, my precious girl.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.670
Kuchiha...

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.710
You will die before you blossom.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.630
My poor girl.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.680
This is creepy.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.560
Shh! They'll hear you!

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.060
Leave these here, and they will...

00:02:55.610 --> 00:03:01.030
Thank you for the food every...

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.380
The filth will curse you!

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:25.220
Time after time, I've told you
to come in through the front door.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.350
He's still an outrageous, crappy monk.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.060
Yo! Here comes the crappy monk.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.480
Don't be afraid. Bring some tea!

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.650
You should be saying,
"May I have some tea?"

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.320
Oh, dear.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.450
So?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.320
You like this?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.450
Did you transform from outrageous
to self-reproving?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.040
I must travel far for my new job.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.460
New job...

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.250
Exterminating demons?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.050
Yup.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.260
I heard that an inugami appeared or something.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.180
This is good.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:11.180
And what does that inugami have to do
with you shaving your head?

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.600
Everything.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.730
If I look like a monk, people will provide alms for my travel expenses.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.740
By the way, Shamon...

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.610
Have you thought any more about our deal?

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:27.160
I won't work under you, Tadajirou.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:31.120
I can't stand just looking good
to the bigwigs, even as a favor to you.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.120
Give up on it.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.790
Tadajirou, listen to me.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.710
You can still give up your current position.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.920
It'd be better if you did,

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:42.800
even if you took a pay cut
and had to do extra work!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:47.550
You can't deal with demons
if you can't see them!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.470
That will only endanger your life!

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.520
Then...

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.520
you'd help me if I learned to sense demons?

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.020
You couldn't possibly...

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:08.620
Then think about it again
when you come back.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:09.370
Wait!

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.790
Listen to me!

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.290
It's such a fine day.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:19.290
The world is very beautiful.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.300
Don't go beyond your capacity, Tadajirou.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.510
Yes, I know.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.970
Now, now, get going.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.260
Have a safe trip.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.430
Tadasaburou.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.020
Y-Yes.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.480
Don't bother seeing me off.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.520
I will!

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.480
I don't want you leaving
footprints on the white wall

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.020
or breaking the shingles!

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.280
And it's hard to explain things to officers when they mistake you for a burglar.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.160
I'm so sorry.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.450
The god Sannou's dog

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:56.830
likes red clothes very much.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.920
Last night, I was invited to a harvest festival.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:05.970
There, I had a first drink, sip, sip...

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.560
Do you live here?

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.570
Where did she go?

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.830
Ryouhin ryouchi nimo seikaiun irematsu chuujou seishuu kuusha!

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.010
If you kill me,

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.550
she'll die too.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.720
You must be the demon hunter that the villagers sent for.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.310
I protected them for many moons,

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.100
but now they are returning
my favor with hatred.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.690
I cannot survive without her body,

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.900
and she cannot survive without me.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.700
She's a poor girl.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.570
I'll show you what you get
for trying to kill her and me!

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.120
You'll have no place in this village,

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:18.620
even if you... kill me!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.590
Please, Buddha!

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.090
Kanji zai bosatsu gyoujin hannya hara mitaji.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.930
Shouken go on kai kuu doissai kuyaku.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.220
Sharishi shiki fui kuu kuu fui shiki.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:37.720
Shiki soku zekuu...

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.320
Inflicting violence on a child
is an evil act for a monk.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:50.360
Then if she weren't a child,
you'd kill without hesitation?

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:54.370
I have to, when it's a monster
that harms people!

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.490
That's why I was called in.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.660
And only people get to live?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.830
People's lives are so valuable, huh?

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.170
No life is more valuable than any other.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.840
All lives must be treated equally.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.180
Then why do people despise us?

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:17.140
Humans, her own kind, despise her.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.640
They worship her as a god when it's convenient,

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:22.140
and when it's not, they attack her as a demon.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.650
And as always, you humans bring the violence.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.150
Why do you exterminate demons?

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:33.650
Because saving people is a good deed.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.370
A good deed, huh?

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.370
How ridiculous!

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:42.910
Demons have rules against harming people,

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:46.330
and people are at fault too.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.670
Can't you see that?

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:52.170
The selfishness of human action
is all there in your "good deeds"!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:57.850
A world where people and demons can understand each other is nothing but a dream.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.390
Kill! Kill!

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.680
Kill all the demons!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:06.020
Monk, you will not see peace
unless you kill all the demons.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:09.270
Now, save this girl with your own hands.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.530
We have no place to go anymore.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.950
But you and the villagers lived together peacefully until now.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:17.990
Then...

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.580
And now you are here,
right in front of me.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.540
That's the answer.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:28.540
All I want is for this girl to live in peace.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.550
But the villagers won't allow even that.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.430
Would you entrust the girl to me?

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.060
Stop talking nonsense!

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.640
It's what I really want.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.190
I want to take her out of here.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:52.860
She will never find peace,
even if you take her far away from here.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.610
That's not necessarily true.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:59.200
Because inside the barrier at my temple, you won't be able to emerge.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.330
You're going to seal me?

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.660
Only in the temple.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.790
When she steps outside,
it will be the same as now,

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.670
but it should lessen the burden on her.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:12.340
You're going to keep an eye on her,
now that the villagers are done with me.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.760
Not just keep an eye on her.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:15.800
Watch over her, with you.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:20.260
People and demons are equal.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:24.350
If we can't come to an agreement, we must
compromise with each other and keep trying,

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.520
until we can find a middle ground.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.900
I'll leave the decision about
what to do with her to you.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.490
Don't worry.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:43.990
I won't harm you.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.380
Do you want to leave this village
and come with me?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.340
This brought me no money at all,

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.810
but perhaps I found something more valuable.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.600
I don't really understand...

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:17.440
what a good deed actually is.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:23.410
So I think I'll try to keep
the people around me smiling.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.410
That's all I can do.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:30.410
At least I can drink cheerfully
as long as I do that.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.540
And that's enough.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.500
Now, let's go home.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.170
Hey! Don't cling to my legs!

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:46.100
I always thought I was quite worthless.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.520
There's nothing more troublesome than being the third son in a samurai family.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.850
I can't go up or go down.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.190
At best, I'll be adopted by another family.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:12:01.490
For that reason, and because I could see demons from birth, I chose to become a monk.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:02.860
Hey.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.870
I heard you're a good cook,
despite being so young,

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.370
Kosen-san.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:08.740
Right.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.250
I just wanted to be useful to others.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:27.810
H-Hey, wait! Where did you come from?!

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.890
That's a prohibited area!

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:31.980
Is it?

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:32.940
I'm sorry.

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:36.150
I saw a rare bird, and I forgot.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:38.150
Scales...

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:41.940
Do you happen to have demonic traits?

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.660
What if I do?

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.950
I'll ask you to leave!

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:52.660
What if I refuse?

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.170
In that case, to the best of my abilities...

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:58.670
To the best of your abilities?

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.750
I'll go get some help!

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:05.970
What?!

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:07.430
Yes, I suck!

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.310
It's only been a week since I came here.

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:13.680
I don't know anything about
demon extermination.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.190
I'm sorry.

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:16.810
And don't worry.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:19.440
These are only a demon's curse.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.940
Fine, then.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.900
So you're new here.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:26.950
What's your name?

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:28.660
I'm Kosen.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:33.200
You seem to have studied a lot about demons, Kosen-san.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:37.790
Your supporting temple must have opposed you coming here.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.920
Well, yes.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:42.250
I'm sixteen years old.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.960
I'm still a youngster.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:48.470
I only stopped tying my hair a few days ago,
but... please take me in!

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:53.470
Gankei-sama has told me that this is the best place to learn about demon hunting.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.020
Enough of the formal introductions.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:58.480
Come on in! Okay?

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.150
Do you happen to be drunk?

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:05.530
No way!

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:07.110
I'm... not...

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.870
Ouch.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.700
Shamon-sama.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.500
Are you awake now, Shamon-sama?

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:25.210
I think you put him into an eternal sleep.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.470
Let me show you around.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:33.140
It's a dirty place, so forgive me.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:35.930
I'm disappointed...

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.140
that you're a person like this.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.850
You're completely corrupted!

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:44.360
Has the sharp edge of your
Suimou Sword been dulled?!

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:47.860
We monks should live modestly!

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:52.240
You seem to like memorizing scripture.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:55.990
What would a sloppy man like you
know about anything?

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.250
Saburo! Are you out of your mind?!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:02.420
You're ruining your life
with fantasies and delusions!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.340
I'm not asking you to understand!

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:07.800
I wasn't going to argue with you, because you can't see demons!

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:11.220
I have a rare ability that you don't.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:12.590
I want to use that ability.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.300
Saburo! Listen to me!

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:17.560
I will not be your chess piece!

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.350
Why won't you let me do what I want?!

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:24.480
You're from a family of samurai, but you left your family?

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.070
Y-Yes.

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:31.410
But isn't demon hunting about
the only thing you can learn here?

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:32.910
That's exactly what I want.

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:36.540
If I can save people
with the skills I learn here,

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.040
that will be my good deed.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.790
Is demon hunting a good deed?

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.290
Of course it is!

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.710
Avoid the evil deeds,
and do good to people.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:49.720
That's important in order
to live as a human.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:53.010
You are very knowledgeable about scripture.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.720
Well, I've studied more than most, I believe.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:01.770
Are you telling me I haven't studied enough?!

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.310
Then let me ask you!

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:06.190
What's the true meaning of Zen?!

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:08.730
Let me see...

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.240
It's like the chopsticks we use every day.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.450
Chopsticks?!

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:14.950
Stop ridiculing me!

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.450
I've renounced being obsessed with Zen.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.660
Zen is just a tool, like chopsticks.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:26.210
Usually, we don't realize how useful it is.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.590
Our values won't change
just because we can use it.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:34.930
Even if you've done many good deeds through demon hunting,

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.470
if you have ideas like that...

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:40.470
Demon hunting is not a good deed.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.560
It's a very useful way to earn a living.

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.730
It provides the financial resources
we can't do without.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:48.110
What are you seeking from monks?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.360
Please excuse me.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.450
I won't stay here for my apprenticeship!

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.860
Kosen-dono,

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.950
visit Sakagami Shrine.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.990
Uneducated, you will be confused.

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:03.460
Learn, and there is no good or evil.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.870
After a thousand winters,
the pine tree never changes,

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:09.380
and in the spring, it blossoms
again, despite its age.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.300
That's my ideal.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.470
Keep that in mind.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.140
Shamon-sama?

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:21.810
Sorry, sorry.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.480
Don't worry. He's gone now.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:27.310
Hey, wanna go out for soba?

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:37.200
...I was plowing through the enemy.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.870
But the enemy wouldn't go away so easily.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.790
I thought it'd be a long battle,
so I got ready for that.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.830
And I...

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.500
What about the visitor earlier?

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:48.790
He was disappointed with me and left.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:52.250
I think he'd find my preaching
at him unbearable.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:56.510
I think you're very admirable.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.680
Yeah? Oh, yeah?

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.720
Man, really!

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.690
Zen monks and children are
actually the same thing.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.400
Preaching alone isn't good enough.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.860
They must find the truth for themselves.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:18.200
Since when did demon hunting become
a source of income instead of a good deed?

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.700
Well...

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.780
He's just like you used to be.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.410
Perhaps so.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.960
Let me warn you of one thing.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:31.420
If your ideals are too high,
your life will be difficult later on.

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.590
I made you worry, huh?

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:37.130
Sorry.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.970
As if I'd ever worry about you!

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:43.850
It's just that she'd be sad
if you got in trouble.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:46.390
That's why I want to overcome this challenge.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.860
No matter how much I'm confused about humans and demons,

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:55.860
I want to accept them as they are
and keep moving forward.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:59.450
Uneducated, you will be confused.

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:01.660
Learn, and there is no good or evil.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.240
Those must be words of Zen.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.660
What do they mean?

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:08.540
If I'm not confused by the difference between good and evil

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.040
and accept them as they are,

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.880
my preferences will no longer matter.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:17.130
Not confused by the difference
between good and evil?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:20.220
That's a little different from
what you said earlier.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.140
Which is right?

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:25.010
I don't know.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.140
No matter how many books I read,

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.600
I can't come up with an answer!

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:35.150
So you came here, looking for certainty?

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:41.530
But I don't think the answer can be found in this shrine either.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.200
What are you doing here?

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:49.870
Sasaki-sama!

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.710
Sasaki-sama, you were here?

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.750
Please excuse my interruption.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.710
Everyone is looking for you.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:58.460
I see.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.630
Then please excuse me.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.760
U-Um, who might you be?

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:09.060
If that is the teaching of Zen,

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:13.770
then I'm probably the person
who's most distant from it.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.730
No, that's me.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.740
What are you seeking from monks?

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:29.790
And I'm still worthless.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:37.750
Give up, and you'll die, fledgling.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:40.550
If you give up thinking about your troubles,

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:43.760
you'll even forget that you are human.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:47.640
A bird?

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:55.350
By the way, I heard that you prepared
the room and the chest cloth for Kuchiha.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.440
Yeah.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:59.730
Did you come all the way here
just to check on that?

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:03.240
It was half for my appetite
and half for my curiosity.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:09.280
I wanted to meet the unique monk
who'd been so kind to a very violent demon.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.250
Don't you hate that inugami woman?

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.420
I was told that she was a guest, so I treated her accordingly.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.750
If she was sick, I just helped her.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:21.000
The priestesses would not
approve of those acts.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.630
Probably.

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:23.880
You really <i>are</i> a monk.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.050
Very admirable.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.550
Thank you.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:28.510
By the way...

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:30.560
you're disturbing my work.

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:32.270
Don't mind me.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.480
Hey, dude, this tastes great.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.390
It's bamboo shoot from Meguro.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:40.070
Hey, give me a hand over here.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.480
Yes, sir!

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:44.900
Stop playing around!

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:47.360
Hey, here comes the demon lord.
